      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty strong comparison. but aren't there some modern democracies that use different systems for different things? like, i know some places have a head of state that isn't elected directly by everyone. is it really universally seen as \"wrong\" or \"unacceptable\" to have an indirect system, or is it just that the US version is seen as particularly outdated?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
